{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact readable-diff design head c372ea0399aa07b32896d065f132c0bf65aa642b on builder/readable-diff-design-20261102, for request 353a0ec0 and review request b08498d6.\n\nThe gap from bfb0c27e is closed. Commit 4fecb193 changes only proposal.css and the three HTML sources. Each gutter column is now `calc(var(--line-digits)*1ch + 8px)`, set per patch from its largest line number, and the cells no longer wrap. The recaptured ten-file key render shows 355, 356 and 357 on one line each. The new browser check opens every file and context disclosure and requires each line number to sit on one line inside its cell. It checks 4,112 cells across the twelve width, theme and case combinations, and none fails. Run against the old renders, the same check finds 200 failing cells at each width, so it catches the defect I reported. Rows still match DATA (497, 13 and 407 per case), with no outer overflow, page errors or outside requests. render.exit reads \"exit 0\".\n\nScope. Main f277867f is an ancestor. The head still adds only fourteen paths, all under notes/, and the worktree is clean. Since 75b64f90, the DATA files, README and card-frame.css are unchanged. Two key PNGs change, and the collapsed truncated key stays byte-identical because it shows no gutter. The commit-message check passes for all three commits.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to 42e45dea…d5c825ccc327b. It covers 318 files in two units: the original 267-file unit, unchanged, and a 51-file gutter unit. All 318 files match, and all 31 table digests match their units. SHA256SUMS passes in both units and in the review directory, whose SHA256SUMS hashes to 753e1ae9…11176c7da5. Its four checks read \"exit 0\", no evidence file is writable, and the credential-pattern scan finds nothing.\n\nBindings. The three artifacts rest on promise 5e63db87 and assert a63f7698 only, so none is stale. Ruling 09a2b61a appears in the text.\n\nThe rest of my review in bfb0c27e stands: the measured renderer choice, the under-claims for base changes and truncation, the labeled provenance, and the separate Projection and Display budgets meet 353a0ec0 under 09a2b61a and a63f7698.\n\nArchitecture: sound as a proposal. Folding stays local to the card, and completeness and omission stay with the server. Security: no finding. The pages hold no script and make no outside request, the read buttons are inactive, and private fixture output stays outside the units. Simplification: no change needed. The gutter rule is one CSS variable per patch.\n\nLimits stay explicit: no product renderer, schema or dependency changes, no Goose Desktop claim (1a44f042), and the held cut-short answer stays with e4d0cfed. The planner shows Hugh the landed renders, and Hugh decides before any build.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f2dac5274e5b48a73edd953d9245a4141392c7d","binding":"assigned","head":"c372ea0399aa07b32896d065f132c0bf65aa642b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:282a692bbb0e5e9d3fb21b49b78ee63dc75ba894\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5e63db87aa26c3d72b8c5a512fbb2fd83480cc47\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:282a692bbb0e5e9d3fb21b49b78ee63dc75ba894","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}